name chess-com-games
match *.pgn
# PGN packaging uses formats/pgn.format; chess.c applies the legal board rules.
# Every game is a record [line, tags, layer]; its
# line the trajectory of positions and moves, replayed under firmware/chess.firmware by the Variant it names; every
# tag a statement [name, value] as written; its clock comments ([%clk]) its layer. chess.com's archive is of games
# played: a record with variations or NAGs would be an annotator's study and is said as one.
grammar pgn
records played
# Completed played games attest [position_before, canonical_move, position_after]
# with the result scored for the side making the move; * attests no outcome.
